# [1.0.0] : 2026-11-16

* New ipuz plugin (read and write)
* Richer crossword model:
  * Clues are Clue objects with enumerations, explanations, hints, concise
    versions, linked clues, labels and cells, plus clues without a
    direction; exolve reads and writes all of these
  * Marked definitions in clues (exolve ~{...}~ and ~{{class}...}~), which
    round-trip through exolve and are written as plain text in other formats
  * Squares can be circled, coloured, highlighted, diagramless, have a given
    letter, a label instead of a number, or corner text, or be outside the
    grid (void)
  * Puzzle metadata: editor, publisher, publication, date, difficulty, url,
    id, explanation, postscript, credits, email, origin, language
  * Ninas, extra questions, final answers, hints for wrong answers, and
    alternative answers
* Enumerations can count words or letters, e.g. (8, 2 words), (two words),
  (7, 2w), (6 letters), or be (?), (abbr.) or (acronym), following exolve's
  rules for which parenthesised group is the enumeration
* Bars are stored once, in XWord#bars, and read and changed with
  XWord#bar? and XWord#set_bar; Cell#borders, Cell#has_bar? and
  XWord#mirror_bars! are removed
* ipuz: read and write bars
* AcrossLite binary: read and write circled squares (GEXT)
* qxw: read cutouts as squares outside the grid
* exolve: decorators (@ * ! ~), colours, ninas, questions, alternatives,
  credits, explanations, postscript and other metadata; multi-line
  preludes; clues are matched to the grid by number
* Warnings about unsupported features now cover all of the above, not just
  bars

# [0.7.0] : 2026-11-15

* Barred grids: read bars from qxw files, and read and write them in exolve
  grids
* Clue numbering and word extraction treat bars as word boundaries
* Warn when converting to a format that cannot represent a feature of the
  crossword (currently bars); pangrid -l shows which plugins support which
  features

# [0.6.1] : 2026-11-14

* Clue files (-c): ignore comment lines starting with #, such as the
  header qxw adds to its answer files

# [0.6.0] : 2026-11-14

* Add a -c/--clues option to add clues from a text file to the input
  crossword
* Remove the web frontend (and the webrick dependency)
* AcrossLite binary: convert text to and from ISO-8859-1 (fixes accented
  characters), don't duplicate rebus sections when re-writing a puzzle, and
  reject scrambled or truncated files
* Exolve reader: strip clue numbers, read the setter as the author and the
  prelude as the preamble, and infer the grid size when it isn't given
* Reddit reader: more robust clue parsing
* Exolve and Reddit readers share the same clue number stripping, which
  leaves linked clues like "1, 5 Clue" intact
* CSV reader: honour the Offset header
* JSON: keep rebus squares on a round trip, and validate input
* Excel writer: support rebus squares
* Writers no longer crash on puzzles without clues
* A missing optional gem no longer stops other plugins from loading
* Command line: exit with status 1 on errors, report format errors without a
  backtrace, and use binary file I/O (fixes binary formats on Windows)
* Replace the vendored Trollop with OptionParser; declare the chunky_png and
  csv dependencies
* Library: XWord is no longer an OpenStruct, so unknown attributes raise
  NoMethodError; across_clues/down_clues default to []; XWord#number clears
  stale clue numbers

# [0.5.3] : 2024-11-27

* Improve the qxw reader

# [0.5.2] : 2022-02-20

* Add settings for using the PNG writer as a library
* Minor fix for exolve reader plugin

# [0.5.1] : 2022-02-04

